RECORDED DEVIATIONS (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Output path: the prompt's "Output" lists apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**, but
   the established, BUILDING convention (every DONE sibling: AutomationsListPage, AutomationCard,
   AutomationActivityFeed, admin/*, analytics/*) lives under apps/apple/Sources/Features/
   Automations/**, which project.yml globs into the iOS + macOS app targets. Files are placed
   there so they compile + are enumerated (xcodegen: 96 pbxproj refs).
2. Filename + type collisions with a PRE-EXISTING, unrelated artifact: the feature-views layer
   already ships a separate `PresetGallery` surface (TeslaSync/feature-views/PresetGallery.*),
   declaring public `AutomationTriggerKind`, `AutomationPresetItem`, and a `PresetGalleryPhase`
   also collided with TeslaSync/feature-views/AlertMessageEditor.Models.swift. Swift compiles one
   module, so filenames AND public type names must be unique. Resolved by naming the page files
   PresetGalleryPage*.swift and the page's own types uniquely (PresetTriggerKind / PresetGalleryItem
   / PresetGalleryCategory / PresetGalleryResponse / PresetGalleryDataSource / PresetGalleryLoadPhase
   / PresetGalleryState / PresetGalleryModel / PresetGalleryCard / PresetGalleryPage / …). All 16
   verified collision-free against the whole target. The web hook name `useAutomationPresets` is
   kept verbatim at the Swift call site (parity requirement).
3. Web route is (unrouted): the web source is the preset-template grid the /automations preset
   disclosure renders inline, not a standalone route. So no top-level AppRoute is claimed (scope
   creep); the screen is exposed as a typed NavigationDestination (PresetGalleryLink) + a
   …RouteRegistration factory, mirroring the DONE sibling AutomationCard / AutomationActivityFeed.
4. Error state: the web treats a failed query as its empty state (data undefined -> presetList = []).
   Per ADR-013 ("never a blank region") a distinct retryable error state was ADDED (TSQueryError +
   refresh). The 3 REQUIRED states (loading / empty / success) are all implemented; error is additive.
5. Install action: the web navigates to the typed builder pre-filled (/automations/new?preset=id),
   a separate parity unit. Exposed as the injected onInstall shell hook (default no-op), mirroring
   the sibling pages' onCreate/onNavigate seams — a real wired button to an out-of-scope destination.
6. No SSE / staleness chip: useAutomationPresets is a STATIC query (web staleTime: STATIC), not a
   live source, so ADR-013's >2-min staleness indicator does not apply here.

