DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI PresetGallery shipped at parity with the web source: an
@Observable PresetGalleryModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injected
PresetGalleryDataSource whose method name mirrors the ported web hook verbatim
(useAutomationPresets(category:)). The page reproduces the web responsive preset-card grid — a
loading state (a grid of skeleton cards), a clock empty state (automations.presets.empty), and a
fade-in + index-staggered success grid of preset cards (icon box, name, trigger-label subtitle,
action-count badge, 2-line description, full-width Install) — built on the P2 tokens + P3 shared
components (TSGlassPanel / TSCard / TSButton / TSBadge / TSIconBox / TSEmptyState / TSQueryError /
TSSkeleton / TSFadeIn / TSStaggerItem), no hand-rolled glass; adaptive macOS/iPad (multi-column)
vs iPhone-compact (single column); every visible string from Localizable.xcstrings with the web
key names; VoiceOver labels/traits + Dynamic Type + light/dark. A retryable error state was added
per ADR-013. Verified on BOTH idioms by real iOS-18 + macOS-15 Swift 6 strict-concurrency
type-checks (0/0 on the surface) and an executed 19/19 model harness. The full xcodebuild scheme is
RED (BUILD_EXIT=65) ONLY due to the pre-existing, out-of-scope result-builder error in
shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift — reproduced identically on a clean baseline without my
changes (forbidden to commit-fix) — the identical disposition under which the sibling P7 pages were
accepted DONE.

